      "rationale": "The report says formatting an invalid/incomplete WHERE clause currently raises `ValueError: None is not in list`, which comes from sqlparse's internal token-index bookkeeping (sql.py's TokenList.insert_before/token_index used while reindenting a Where group, or its group_where/_groupable_tokens computation) when it cannot locate an expected token for an incomplete WHERE clause. sqlparse has always been documented and tested (e.g. the historic issue121/issue26 regression tests) to tolerate malformed SQL without crashing and without dropping input tokens, so the expected values -- no exception, and the trailing \"where\"/original text preserved -- come directly from that long-standing, still-intended behavior rather than from the current buggy output. The third test is a control on a well-formed WHERE clause to make sure the fix does not regress normal reindent formatting.",
